{"text": "Lorillard\n\nMEMORANDUM\n\nJanuary 5, 1989\nTo: A. B. Hudson\n\nFROM: E. FP. DeLaura\n\nAttached are the Low Tar panel results for the Harley\nLights II retest. Results are compared with the original\nHLIT test which was conducted in June, 1988.\n\none of the key purposes for the retest was to monitor PM\nsmokers\u2019 reactions toward the product which when first\ntested were quite favorable.\n\nPlease note this HLII retest is not an aged or changed\nformula from when originally tested.\n\nThe retest product maintained its favorable acceptance and\nperformance in total and particularly anong the critical Pa\nsmokers.\n\nThe HLII product, overall, nets out as a well balanced,\nsmooth product. \u2018Although\u2019 the harsh tasting level at 31 is\nsomewhat high, additional measures such bitterness,\nunpleasant aftertaste and the desire to be milder are low\nand indicate no underlying negatives.\n\nIf you have any questions, please call.\n\nLD\n\nEB. F. D.\nfee\nD:PRRLII/57\nattach.\ncc: B. Deaton \u20ac. Be Ray\nS$. T. Jones H. EL smith ~\nT. HL Mau G. R. Telford\n\nA. P. Pasheluk H. H. Westphalen\n\n6PLEGPSS",
